    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d287-a3">

                <pb facs="0461" n="419" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg419"/>

                <head>Earl Russell to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-09-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 8, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Lord Russell presents his compliments to Mr. Adams, and has the honor to inform
                    him that instructions have been issued which will prevent the departure of the
                    two iron-clad vessels from Liverpool.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
